kbuild: put .config back in the headers package

Ubuntu's own linux-headers-<version>-generic ships
/usr/src/linux-headers-<version>/.config; the headers package this
repository builds does not, because bindeb-pkg goes through
scripts/package/install-extmod-build, which copies
include/config/auto.conf and include/config/kernel.release and stops
there. Out-of-tree modules that read .config directly, as several
vendor and DKMS trees do, therefore find on Ubuntu's kernel a file
they do not find on this one.

Kbuild itself does not need it: scripts/Makefile.modinst reads
CONFIG_MODULE_SIG_HASH and CONFIG_MODULE_SIG_KEY from auto.conf, which
is already in the package. This only closes the difference with the
kernel Raye mirrors. Nothing is added to the kernel and nothing runs
differently; the file names the signing key's path, not the key, which
auto.conf already names.

From XanMod's 7.0 series.

--- a/scripts/package/install-extmod-build
+++ b/scripts/package/install-extmod-build
@@ -48,6 +48,9 @@
 	fi
 } | tar -c -f - -T - | tar -xf - -C "${destdir}"
 
+# copy .config manually to be where it's expected to be
+cp "${KCONFIG_CONFIG}" "${destdir}/.config"
+
 # When ${CC} and ${HOSTCC} differ, rebuild host programs using ${CC}.
 #
 # This caters to host programs that participate in Kbuild. objtool and
